<title>FRANCE: France revises down '97 beet sowings estimate.</title>
<headline>France revises down '97 beet sowings estimate.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French farm ministry on Wednesday cut its estimate for 1997 sugar beet sowings to 454,000 hectares from 455,000 hectares forecast last month.</p>
<p>In its second estimate for the new beet harvest, the ministry said area sown to sugar beet would fall by 0.8 percent from a revised 458,000 hectares in 1996.</p>
<p>As of May 1 some 98 percent of the area had been sown to sugar beet.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
